# NON-EXECUTABLE ANNOTATED MALBOLGE MODULE SCAFFOLD.
#
# Module: doom.host.v1.abi
# Generated-from: cli/adapters/doom/abi.h
# Intended artifact: cli/adapters/doom/abi.malbolge
#
# This file intentionally contains no canonical Malbolge bytes yet. It reserves
# the guest-side module identity for version-one DOOM capability call frames.
# The future C-to-Malbolge pipeline must generate and verify this module from the
# deterministic ABI contract rather than hand-translating declarations.
#
# Runtime rule: a .malbolge capsule declaring doom.host.v1 must cause the CLI or
# runtime linker to load this module automatically. Ordinary Malbolge programs
# must not receive DOOM capabilities implicitly.
#
# Debug telemetry capability 0x0600 accepts language, source identity, execution
# location, and the active instruction text. A Malbolge executor reports
# language=MALBOLGE, source=<artifact>, location=<cell/address>, and the current
# graphical instruction byte so the host title can display real execution.
#
# Blocked by: versioned-host-capability-call-abi, state-aware-malbolge-linker,
# cross-platform-native-capability-runners, and C-to-Malbolge code generation.
